$search — web search via DuckDuckGo (results as JSON in texts[])

  $search
  $search(limit=10, lang='en', region='us')
  $search(limit=5, fetch_pages=True, fetch_max=3)

  Alias: $serch (same handler)

  INPUT
    prompts[] — search query (one result JSON per prompt)

  OUTPUT
    texts[] — JSON array of objects per query:
      { "url": "...", "text": "title/snippet [+ page body when fetched]" }
    Optional fields when fetch_pages is enabled:
      "page_text" — cleaned plain text extracted from the page
      "page_fetch" — "ok", "error: …", or "skipped: fetch_max"

  ARGUMENTS
    limit=           — max search hits (default 10, max 100)
    lang=, region=   — DuckDuckGo locale (or AH_SEARCH_KL=us-en)
    site=            — restrict to site:domain
    timeout=         — search HTTP timeout seconds (default 60)
    fetch_pages=     — 1/true/yes — download result pages and merge cleaned text
    fetch_max=       — max pages to download (default 3, capped by limit)
    fetch_timeout=   — per-page download timeout seconds (default 15)
    fetch_max_chars= — max characters per page after cleaning (default 12000)

  Page fetch removes scripts, nav/footer/aside, cookie banners, ads (heuristic),
  then appends readable body to each result's "text" under "--- page ---".

  ENVIRONMENT
    AH_EMULATE_SEARCH=1 | AH_EMULATE_SERCH=1 — placeholder JSON, no network
    AH_SEARCH_KL=us-en — override kl for HTML search

  EXAMPLES
    @news: $search(limit=5)
    latest AI agent frameworks 2026

    @deep: $search(limit=8, fetch_pages=True, fetch_max=4)
    UK renewable energy policy 2026

  Prompt-consuming: Yes.
